<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: PRAGUE BREWERIES POSTS CZK135.3MLN H1 LOSS.</title>
<headline>PRAGUE BREWERIES POSTS CZK135.3MLN H1 LOSS.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech brewer Prazske Pivovary</p>
<p>a.s. , 55 percent owned by Britain's Bass plc ,</p>
<p>said on Monday that it posted a pre-tax first half loss of</p>
<p>135.34 million crowns.</p>
<p>Results for six month period ending June 30, 1997 (in</p>
<p>millions of crowns for financial results and thousands of</p>
<p>hectolitres for output) according to Czech accounting</p>
<p>standards.</p>
<p>					H1 1997		H1 1996</p>
<p>DOMESTIC OUTPUT</p>
<p> (thousands of hectolitres)   1,032		  1,096</p>
<p> EXPORTS				207		    173</p>
<p> TOTAL OUTPUT		     1,239		  1,269</p>
<p>TOTAL TURNOVER</p>
<p> (millions of crowns)	   1,161.404	    1,096.408</p>
<p> OPERATING PROFIT		   -15.482		 45.738</p>
<p> RESULT FOR PERIOD		 -135.342		-36.239</p>
<p>NOTE: The brewery added in a note: &quot;Since the existence of the</p>
<p>merged company came into effect as of 1 February, the results</p>
<p>for January 1997 and 1996 do not comprise results of Ostravar</p>
<p>and Vratislavice.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Robin Shepherd, Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
